  "slug": "product-of-array-except-self",
  "title": "Product of Array Except Self",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "Prefix sum",
  "patterns": [
    "prefix sum",
    "prefix product"
  ],
  "lists": [
    "blind-75",
    "grind-75",
    "interview-150"
  ],
  "hints": [
    "dividing the total product by nums[i] would work, but you're not allowed to divide - and it breaks on zeros anyway. what's the product 'except self' made of, structurally?",
    "the product of everything except index i is exactly (product of everything before i) times (product of everything after i)",
    "build a left-to-right pass computing, at each index, the running product of everything strictly before it",
    "then do a right-to-left pass, multiplying each position's existing value by a running product of everything strictly after it"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "including the element itself in the prefix or suffix product",
    "trying to use division as a shortcut, which breaks when the array contains a zero",
    "forgetting to initialize the running prefix/suffix product to 1, not 0"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given an array of integers.\n\n**Return a new array where each position holds the product of every element in the original array except the one at that position.**\n\nDo it without using division.\n",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= nums.length <= 10^5",
      "-30 <= nums[i] <= 30",
      "the product of any prefix or suffix of nums fits in a 32-bit signed integer"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "the array contains a single zero",
      "the array contains multiple zeros (every result becomes 0)",
      "the array contains negative numbers"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
